---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Is List-Unsubscribe the same as the unsubscribe link in my footer?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "No: the footer link is content; the header is metadata clients read to offer a native one-click unsubscribe. Bulk senders need both." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "What happens without it?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Gmail and Yahoo's 2024 sender requirements classify non-compliant bulk mail toward rejection, and complaint rates rise because unsubscribing is harder than reporting spam." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Does one-click unsubscribe need a confirmation page?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "No: confirmation pages defeat the point. One click, immediate opt-out, brief confirmation notice afterwards." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Can I use it for transactional email?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Transactional mail is generally exempt, but including the header harms nothing and respects user choice." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "How do I verify my changes?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Run the record lookup to confirm live values, then check the propagation checker for worldwide agreement. Both tools run in your browser." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "What TTL should I use?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "3600 seconds is the default. Drop to 300 a day before changes so cutover is quick, then restore." } }
  ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="List-Unsubscribe Headers: Requirements and Setup"
  description="The List-Unsubscribe header explained: one-click unsubscribe requirements from Gmail and Yahoo, header syntax, and how ESPs implement it."
  schema={[faqSchema]}
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["Email Authentication", "/email-authentication/"], ["List-Unsubscribe Headers"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">List-Unsubscribe Headers</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">List-Unsubscribe Headers: Requirements and Setup</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The List-Unsubscribe header is a machine-readable unsubscribe instruction inside the email itself. Since 2024 it is effectively mandatory: Gmail and Yahoo require a one-click unsubscribe for bulk senders, and enforcement means rejection, not just spam-foldering.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Unsubscribe methods</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">mailto</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Legacy</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">URL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Modern target</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">RFC 8058 One-Click</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Bulk-sender requirement</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
<nav class="pd-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">On this page</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#what-the-header-looks-like">What the header looks like</a></li>
        <li><a href="#the-pieces">The pieces</a></li>
        <li><a href="#how-it-gets-set-up">How it gets set up</a></li>
        <li><a href="#frequently-asked-questions">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#related">Related</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="what-the-header-looks-like">What the header looks like</h2>
      <pre class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">List-Unsubscribe: &lt;https://example.com/unsub/user-token&gt;, &lt;mailto:unsub@example.com?subject=unsubscribe&gt;
List-Unsubscribe-Post: List-Unsubscribe=One-Click</pre>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="the-pieces">The pieces</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong class="text-ink">URL method:</strong> a link that unsubscribes in one click, without login or confirmation page (that is what List-Unsubscribe-Post: One-Click demands).</li><li><strong class="text-ink">mailto method:</strong> an unsubscribe address the client can email; legacy but still accepted.</li><li>The mail client renders its own native Unsubscribe button from this header, above your content.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="how-it-gets-set-up">How it gets set up</h2>
      <p>You rarely add it by hand: reputable ESPs (Mailchimp, Klaviyo, SendGrid and friends) add the header automatically to campaigns. Your jobs are: keep the unsubscribe landing flow one-click compliant, never require login to unsubscribe, process opt-outs promptly, and verify the header exists on your live mail (view original message, check the headers).</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is List-Unsubscribe the same as the unsubscribe link in my footer?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: the footer link is content; the header is metadata clients read to offer a native one-click unsubscribe. Bulk senders need both.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens without it?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Gmail and Yahoo's 2024 sender requirements classify non-compliant bulk mail toward rejection, and complaint rates rise because unsubscribing is harder than reporting spam.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does one-click unsubscribe need a confirmation page?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: confirmation pages defeat the point. One click, immediate opt-out, brief confirmation notice afterwards.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I use it for transactional email?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Transactional mail is generally exempt, but including the header harms nothing and respects user choice.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I verify my changes?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Run the record lookup to confirm live values, then check the propagation checker for worldwide agreement. Both tools run in your browser.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What TTL should I use?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">3600 seconds is the default. Drop to 300 a day before changes so cutover is quick, then restore.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink" id="related">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/why-emails-go-to-spam/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Gmail and Yahoo sender requirements →</a></li><li><a href="/why-emails-go-to-spam/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Why emails go to spam →</a></li><li><a href="/email-deliverability/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Email deliverability hub →</a></li><li><a href="/gmail-yahoo-bulk-sender-requirements/">Gmail and Yahoo bulk sender requirements</a>, where one-click is mandated</li><li><a href="/why-emails-go-to-spam/">Why emails go to spam</a>, the reputation factors behind placement</li><li><a href="/email-header-analyzer/">Email header analyzer</a>, inspect the headers on real mail</li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
